# LF line endings

Repository policy: [`.gitattributes`](.gitattributes) sets `* text eol=lf`. Every file you create or rewrite must use **LF** (`\n`), never **CRLF** (`\r\n`).

## Hard rules

1. Write tools and editors must emit LF. Do not rely on Windows defaults.
2. After creating or bulk-editing text files, verify no `\r\n` was introduced.
3. Do not change an existing file's line-ending style unless the task requires it.
4. Binary files are exempt; everything else is text unless proven otherwise.

## Quick check

```sh
git diff --check
grep -rl $'\r' --include='*.go' --include='*.md' --include='*.py' .
```

Fix any CRLF before commit.
